This module covers the basics of Internet Control Message Protocol (ICMP). I learned how ICMP is used to send error messages and diagnostic information between network devices.

Topics Covered
Internet Control Message Protocol (ICMP)
ICMP messages
Echo Request and Echo Reply
The ping command
Traceroute
Network connectivity testing
Basic network troubleshooting

What I Learned
ICMP is used to report network errors and provide diagnostic information.
The ping command uses ICMP Echo Request and Echo Reply messages to test connectivity.
Echo Request messages are sent to check whether a destination can respond.
Echo Reply messages are returned when the destination responds to the request.
Traceroute uses different techniques to discover the path packets take through a network.
ICMP helps network administrators identify connectivity problems.

